## Context

At Cimory Group, overtime was handled through chat messages and manual Excel recaps. Overtime management is not only about recording working hours: it involves submission, location verification, multi-level approvals, notifications, and reporting that has to be consistent and traceable.

## Problem

Before the system, HR had to request tap-in and tap-out data from HR Ops, follow up with employees on null records, and look for supporting proof for each null entry. Each recap took about 4 hours.

## My role

Owner: I designed and developed the system end to end, from database design and backend logic to frontend development and deployment.

## As-is analysis

I mapped the process end to end: overtime submission, location check, approval hierarchy, HR administration and reporting.

TODO(content): the as-is process map. Add it with the Diagram component (IN-05).

## Requirements

I translated the operational rules into system logic:

- Location check: GPS coordinates validated against a 100-meter geofence around the office.
- Approval routing by organizational structure, with flexibility for specific cases.
- Approve or reject requests directly from email, using signed tokens.
- Revision requests.
- Automatic rejection of overtime with an actual duration under one hour, notifying the employee and informing the manager.

## Solution design

TODO(content): to-be process and data model (ERD) diagrams (IN-05).

## Build

The system is built with Node.js, Express, PostgreSQL, HTML/JavaScript and Tailwind CSS, with Supabase Storage for files and the Brevo API for email. It generates Excel recaps for HR administration and PDF overtime records with hash-based verification, and accepts proof-of-work photo uploads.

